6. Rewrite the following `if-else-if` ladder using an equivalent `switch` statement in Java:
```java
int tier = 2;
if (tier == 1) {
    System.out.println("Standard Support");
} else if (tier == 2) {
    System.out.println("Priority 24x7 Support");
} else if (tier == 3) {
    System.out.println("Dedicated Enterprise Support");
} else {
    System.out.println("Basic Community Support");
}
```

questions.answer:
**Equivalent `switch` statement:**
```java
int tier = 2;
switch (tier) {
    case 1:
        System.out.println("Standard Support");
        break;
    case 2:
        System.out.println("Priority 24x7 Support");
        break;
    case 3:
        System.out.println("Dedicated Enterprise Support");
        break;
    default:
        System.out.println("Basic Community Support");
        break;
}
```

